      {
        "_uid": "238c6a6d-c6d1-106c-807c-d252193de36d",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Human Rights and Reformist Islam",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "italic"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " translates the influential collection Haqq al-nas which argues for the compatability of human rights and Islam.  ",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Blasphemy and Apostasy in Islam: Debates in Shi'a Jurisprudence",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "italic"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " presents a back and forth debate between two modern Shi'a jurists (one conservative, one reformist) that locates the exact points of controversy surrounding apostasy and blasphemy.",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": " Both books are are published in association with Edinburgh University Press and are available to buy now with a limited offer of a 30% discount using the code NEW30.  ",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
